t have a pung of F1.\n- **Play W2**: Only one W2 remains unseen. Multiple players have discarded W2 (me, across, next), suggesting scarcity. Risky to discard \u2014 possibly useful for chows (W1-W2-W3 or W2-W3-W4). But W3 is fully used up (0 left), making W2 less useful. Likely safe.\n- **Play J2**: J2 is already a full pung ([J2,J2,J2]) by the next player. They clearly completed it and kept discarding around it. So J2 is very safe to discard. I have one \u2014 discarding it poses minimal risk.\n\nReason: Safety is paramount at this stage. J2 has been openly completed as a pung by the next player, meaning they almost certainly won\u2019t use another J2. Other players haven\u2019t shown interest. Meanwhile, keeping J1 (potential dragon pung later), F1 (prevalent wind), or even W4 (possible set) has more strategic value. W2 seems safe due to lack of W3s, but J2 is *definitely* safe because the pung is exposed. Hence, **Play J2** is the safest discard.\n\nAnswer: Play J2"}
